 "method": "- Factor s = geometric mean over the MAVEN/IUVS OH points of observed / edge-corrected model,\n  the method of srcHartley2/i3/reference/i3_rate_scaling.csv. Fitted Q(H2O) = s x input Q(H2O).\n- In the I3 chemistry (i3.conf ChemistryReaction lines) H, OH and O all come from H2O; CO and CO2\n  have no photodissociation channels and only collide. Scaling Q(H2O) by s therefore scales the\n  OH, H and O brightness by s in the optically thin, collisionless limit; the edge-correction\n  factors do not change. Collisional changes in the inner coma at the lower Q are not included.\n- \"Fill-corrected estimate\" of the running new runs: X_now,est = X_earlier,converged x\n  (X_now / X_earlier at the same output) x edge factor of now, for X = OH, H and O; its own factor\n  s_est is fitted to its OH. H is still filling in the new runs, OH and O nearly not\n  (interim_ratio_to_earlier.png).",
